<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles de Sales</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1666">1666</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles de Sales was a French Knight Hospitaller who succeeded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phillippe-de-longvilliers-de-poincy">Philippe de Longvilliers de Poincy</a> as governor of the French part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-kitts">Saint Kitts</a> and the order's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> islands in 1660. He was killed in 1666 fighting the English on Saint Kitts, shortly after the order had sold its rights to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-west-india-company">French West India Company</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After Poincy's death in 1660, <b>Charles de Sales</b> succeeded him.</blockquote><a href="/state/hospitaller-caribbean-colonies">Hospitaller Caribbean colonies</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Thorens-Glières, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=46,6.25&amp;year=1656" aria-label="Thorens-Glières on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4698 544 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Charles de Sales"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5148 814h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5148 814h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=46,6.25&amp;year=1656">What was here in 1656? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
